ree rounds without convergence, with the instruction \"stop and escalate\". That can't be fixed by editing tests. The only proper response is a decision record, so that's what I wrote.\n\nIn the same gate run, every other check passed:\n- 7 tests are mapped to the 7 criteria, and all of them exist.\n- `dotnet build` succeeds and all 7 tests are green.\n- No test that existed before the story was changed.\n\nThe earlier rounds failed because the process running the gate couldn't find `dotnet` (`command not found`), not because of the tests. That problem is gone now.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **`.agents/factory/decisions/CAT-04-01.md`**: the question, the evidence, three options and a recommendation, with no answer.\n- **`tasks/CAT-04/tests.md`**: a new `## needs-human` section pointing to that decision. I didn't touch the tests, the table, the breaks or any production code.\n\n**Your choice in the decision record:**\n1. Accept the test stage as it is.\n2. Reset the round count and run the gate once more, with nothing changed. **This is my recommendation**, if the gate checks breaks at this stage: no gate run has yet confirmed that each break patch under `tasks/CAT-04/breaks/` turns its test red. If it doesn't, option 1 is enough.\n3. Re-plan the story. This only makes sense if you see a problem in the tests; the gate report shows none.\n\nYou can answer it with `/factory-decisions`.","ttft_ms":2130,"type":"result","duration_ms":39549,"uuid":"3b62a909-4a94-4b71-9a15-8b183170b89d","ttft_stream_ms":1701,"time_to_request_ms":34,"first_content_frame_ms":1702,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
